    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is primed for a high-ceiling performance today, anchored by the elite 81.88 efficiency rating of **Gunnar Henderson**. Batting leadoff against Civale, **Gunnar Henderson** gains maximum leverage from his dynamic platoon advantage and a favorable park factor, making him our primary engine for Runs and SB. **Kyle Tucker** (78.94) and **Jackson Merrill** (74.04) follow closely as top-tier plays; **Kyle Tucker** is thriving despite facing a tough arm like Strider due to immense raw talent and prime order placement, while **Jackson Merrill** leverages a significant boost from an aggressive leadoff role against May. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** also remains a standout, as his 73.10 rating is bolstered by a massive 19% SP skill adjustment against the hittable Kochanowicz, providing stability in the heart of the order.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved the final utility spot, where **Miguel Vargas** (54.01) narrowly missed the cut. While **Miguel Vargas** benefited from favorable wind conditions and a solid leadoff-caliber profile, he was edged out by the superior matchup context surrounding our starters, specifically the platoon-advantaged **Josh Lowe** and the surging **Andy Pages**. We are closely monitoring the risk profile for **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks** today; both face left-handed opposition in Snell and Lovelady, respectively, which has compressed their scores into the marginal range. We remain disciplined in sitting **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, and **Nolan Schanuel** despite their respectable projections, as we prioritize maintaining our game-cap flexibility over playing bench pieces against elite arms like Ashcraft. With **Sam Antonacci** seeing an additional 5% wind-out boost in his matchup against Castillo, the stage is set for a high-efficiency day provided our core hitters navigate these mid-tier opposing starters effectively.",
